1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,467
In this video you will install a game three ways: from the microSD card, from a PC

2
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:09,533
over a USB cable, and over MTP by copying a file in Explorer.

3
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:11,533
First, a warning.

4
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:17,067
Installing games you did not buy can get your console banned from Nintendo's online

5
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:19,067
services.

6
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:22,200
Kefir Hub installs NSP, NSZ, XCI and XCZ files.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,400
NSZ and XCZ are compressed; they are unpacked during the install and need more

8
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,400
memory.

9
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:34,800
So start Kefir Hub in Title Mode: hold R while you start a game, or use the Kefir

10
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,800
Hub icon on the HOME Menu.

11
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,200
The first video shows how to add it.

12
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,200
Installing is off at first.

13
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,200
Open Tools, Settings, Install.

14
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:48,667
Choose "Enable sysMMC" or "Enable emuMMC", depending on which one you are running.

15
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:51,000
Read the warning and choose Enable.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,333
"Install location" decides where a game goes: the microSD card or system memory.

17
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:01,800
The default, Automatic, picks the storage that keeps free space on both as even as

18
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,800
possible.

19
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,067
Let's start with the microSD card.

20
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:10,267
Open Tools, File Browser, and go to the folder with your games.

21
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:13,333
To install one file, highlight it and press A.

22
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:15,333
The Install queue opens.

23
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:19,267
It checks the file first and does not install anything yet.

24
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:24,133
For several files, select each one with X, press plus and choose Install.

25
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:29,667
For a whole folder, the same panel has "Install recursively": it finds the packages

26
00:01:29,667 --> 00:01:32,133
in the folder and all its subfolders.

27
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:37,733
At the top of the queue you see how much space is needed and how much is free on the

28
00:01:37,733 --> 00:01:39,733
card and in system memory.

29
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:43,600
Each package shows its size and the storage it will go to.

30
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:48,933
A red package marked "Analysis failed" could not be read: the file is damaged or

31
00:01:48,933 --> 00:01:50,933
incomplete.

32
00:01:50,933 --> 00:01:52,933
You cannot select it.

33
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:56,400
L3 switches the storage for the highlighted package.

34
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:00,200
When everything looks right, press A, "Install selected".

35
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:05,467
During the install you see the package number, overall progress, speed and time

36
00:02:05,467 --> 00:02:07,467
remaining.

37
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:11,400
B skips the current package, and X cancels the whole queue.

38
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,400
Want to keep using Kefir Hub?

39
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,400
Press R3.

40
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:20,933
The queue keeps working in the background and a progress badge stays in the corner.

41
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:23,000
R3 again brings the queue back.

42
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
For a long queue, press minus.

43
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,933
By default a screensaver with a clock and progress appears.

44
00:02:28,933 --> 00:02:32,733
Any button wakes the screen, and the install keeps going.

45
00:02:32,733 --> 00:02:38,267
At the end, the Session summary shows how many packages were installed, skipped and

46
00:02:38,267 --> 00:02:40,267
failed.

47
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:43,467
If something failed, Y shows the list of errors.

48
00:02:43,467 --> 00:02:49,000
If you cancel the queue, finished packages stay installed and the unfinished one is

49
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
removed.

50
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,533
No half-installed game is left behind.

51
00:02:53,533 --> 00:02:55,933
Next, installing from a PC over USB.

52
00:02:55,933 --> 00:03:00,400
You need a cable and a PC app: DBI Backend, ns-usbloader or Fluffy.

53
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,400
We will use DBI Backend Qt.

54
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,400
On the Tools tab press plus.

55
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,533
The Install & Share panel opens.

56
00:03:06,533 --> 00:03:08,533
Choose "PC Install (USB)".

57
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:12,333
The console shows "Waiting for PC" and a USB speed badge.

58
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:14,933
Connect the cable and start the PC app.

59
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:20,400
In the PC app, stream mode must be off, or the console shows "USB session failed".

60
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,867
Add the files and start the transfer.

61
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:28,000
The console receives the list, checks every package and opens the same queue.

62
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Check the storage and press A.

63
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,467
With DBI Backend Qt, the selection, order and storage you set on the PC show up on

64
00:03:35,467 --> 00:03:37,467
the console.

65
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:41,133
This also works for packages that have not started yet.

66
00:03:41,133 --> 00:03:43,600
While PC Install is open, MTP is off.

67
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,600
When you close this screen, it turns back on.

68
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:48,600
The third way is MTP.

69
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:53,733
Connect the console to the PC with a cable in handheld mode, not in the dock.

70
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:58,200
After about two seconds you see "Computer connected — MTP started".

71
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:03,533
If the console does not appear on the PC, press plus on the Tools tab and choose

72
00:04:03,533 --> 00:04:05,533
"Mount MTP".

73
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:10,533
MTP does not start by itself while a USB drive is connected to the console.

74
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:15,933
Right after MTP starts, "Please launch MTP install menu before trying to install"

75
00:04:15,933 --> 00:04:17,933
can show for a moment.

76
00:04:17,933 --> 00:04:22,533
Wait a few seconds, or turn MTP off and on, then copy the file again.

77
00:04:22,533 --> 00:04:25,200
On the PC, open the console in Explorer.

78
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:30,133
There are two drives: the microSD card and "Install (NSP, XCI, NSZ, XCZ)".

79
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:32,667
Copy a game file to the Install drive.

80
00:04:32,667 --> 00:04:38,200
The console installs it while it is being copied, so the file itself is not kept on

81
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,200
the card.

82
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,333
The console opens "MTP Install".

83
00:04:42,333 --> 00:04:47,600
There is no percentage, because the PC does not tell the console the file size.

84
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:51,133
Watch the copy window on the PC to see how far it is.

85
00:04:51,133 --> 00:04:54,400
It closes at about the time the install finishes.

86
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,933
When the file is done you see "MTP install success!".

87
00:04:57,933 --> 00:05:01,000
A few seconds later the Session summary opens.

88
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
B closes it.

89
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:08,267
Note: if you copy a game to the microSD card drive, it is only saved as a file.

90
00:05:08,267 --> 00:05:11,400
You can install it later from the File Browser.

91
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:15,600
To cancel, press X on the console or cancel the copy on the PC.

92
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:20,467
Files that are already installed stay, and the unfinished one is removed.

93
00:05:20,467 --> 00:05:25,933
If you cancel on the console, Windows shows no error: the copy window just closes.

94
00:05:25,933 --> 00:05:31,333
If a game installed but the console says it cannot be started yet, the game needs

95
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:33,333
newer firmware.

96
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,333
Update the firmware and Kefir.

97
00:05:35,333 --> 00:05:37,867
You do not need to reinstall the game.

98
00:05:37,867 --> 00:05:42,000
For more, read the Installing games page in the documentation.

99
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,733
It has separate pages for the microSD card, USB and MTP.
